# Morroblivion's census class quiz, the branch morroblivion_main skips: "Take Quiz" (button 0), ten questions, each
# answered with its first choice (a combat answer), so the script's Player.SetClass names Warrior and the class menu
# opens on it. Starts from morroblivion_main's save after the dock.
# Socucius reads each question aloud (even ClassQuizStage), then its box shows (the odd stage after). The box holds
# the game, so each answer hears the question, lets him finish, and clicks; a button step waits for its box. The
# script tallies a click on its next pass, so a score is waited for.
# Run: python -m tools.live.test_instance questtest --cases <this folder> --load mwtest_mb_chargen_dock --fast --checkpoints --stop-on-fail --timeout 3600
# See docs/commentary/morrowind_runtime.md#a-script-names-the-class

case mbq_offer
walk 0181BCE5
activate 0181BCE5
wait 300
walk 01F8E962
until 1800 fbmwChargen.ClassQuizStage >= 1
wait 120
button 0
end

case mbq_questions_1_to_5
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef On a clear day
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef One Summer afternoon
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef Your cousin has given you
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef heated discussion
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef Your mother sends you to the market
wait 600
button 0
until 300 fbmwChargen.quizScoreCombat >= 5
expect fbmwChargen.quizScoreCombat == 5
end

case mbq_questions_6_to_10
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef While in the marketplace
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef Your father sends you on a task
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef fix the sto
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef the baker gives you
wait 600
button 0
hear 1800 mwSocuciusErgallaRef Entering town
wait 600
button 0
until 300 fbmwChargen.quizScoreCombat >= 10
expect fbmwChargen.quizScoreCombat == 10
end

# Player.SetClass Warrior opens the class menu on Warrior; the pick goes through ChooseClass. Then "Here are the
# results of your class quiz..." waits for its OK. Stage 10's own ShowClassMenu is skipped (the player is no longer
# CharactergenClass), and the birthsign menu follows.
case mbq_class
pick Warrior
button 0
pick The Warrior
until 1800 fbmwChargen.CensusStage >= 6
expect GetStage fbmwChargen >= 20
end
